# Two transports live in this package and they disagree about one dependency:
# the A/B harness (`run.ts`) pins `@anthropic-ai/sdk@0.33`, mirroring the version
# `server/src/adapters/llm/anthropic.ts` is written against, while
# `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` declares a peer on `>=0.93`.
#
# The agent SDK does not actually call into the pinned copy — it talks to the
# Claude Code binary it ships with, and authenticates with your Claude login.
# Bumping the pin to satisfy a peer nothing exercises would silently re-point the
# A/B harness at a different client than the server adapter it mirrors, which is
# the one property that file exists to preserve.
legacy-peer-deps=true
